#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0116 expect=noViolation domain=CO
#note "Rule round 2026-10-12 (owner 2026-10-04: \"compare both values upper case\"; case-insensitive dataset names, 2026-10-01): the BW dataset writes its DOMAIN cell in lower case (bw). Row 1, RDOMAIN=BW: study_domains() upper-cases the DOMAIN cells itself (engine runbook W2 SD), so it matches. Row 2, RDOMAIN=bw: the rule upper-cases RDOMAIN too, so it matches as well. Before upper(RDOMAIN) row 2 fired (bw not in [BW, ...]) - the interim movement the W2 review named."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
dataset CO class="SPECIAL PURPOSE" label="Comments"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col RDOMAIN type=Char label="Related Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col COSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col COVAL   type=Char label="Comment"
---
S1 | CO | BW | 001 | 1 | Comment on body weight
S1 | CO | bw | 001 | 2 | Second comment on body weight
---

dataset BW label="Body Weight"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col BWSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col BWTESTCD type=Char label="Body Weight Test Short Name"
col BWORRES  type=Char label="Result or Finding in Original Units"
---
S1 | bw | 001 | 1 | BW | 250
---
